# OpenClaw .env example
#
# Quick start:
# 1) Copy this file to `.env` (for local runs from this repo), OR to `~/.openclaw/.env` (for launchd/systemd daemons).
# 2) Fill only the values you use.
# 3) Keep real secrets out of git.
#
# Env-source precedence for environment variables (highest -> lowest):
# process env, ./.env, ~/.openclaw/.env, then openclaw.json `env` block.
# Existing non-empty process env vars are not overridden by dotenv/config env loading.
# Note: direct config keys (for example `gateway.auth.token` or channel tokens in openclaw.json)
# are resolved separately from env loading and often take precedence over env fallbacks.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gateway auth + paths
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required if the gateway binds beyond loopback. Leave blank to have OpenClaw
# auto-generate a token on first start, or provide your own using
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. The gateway will refuse to start if this is set to
# the documented example placeholder, so never copy-paste an example value
# from docs or tutorials into this file verbatim.
OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# Optional alternative auth mode (use token OR password).
# OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_PASSWORD=

# Optional path overrides (defaults shown for reference).
# OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=~/.openclaw
# OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=~/.openclaw/openclaw.json
# OPENCLAW_HOME=~

# Optional: import missing keys from your login shell profile.
# OPENCLAW_LOAD_SHELL_ENV=1
# OPENCLAW_SHELL_ENV_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model provider API keys (set at least one)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_KEY=sk-...
# OPENCLAW_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENCLAW_LIVE_GEMINI_KEY=...
# OPENAI_API_KEY_1=...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_1=...
# GEMINI_API_KEY_1=...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...
# OPENAI_API_KEYS=sk-1,sk-2
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEYS=sk-ant-1,sk-ant-2
# GEMINI_API_KEYS=key-1,key-2

# Optional additional providers
# ZAI_API_KEY=...
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=...
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=...
# SYNTHETIC_API_KEY=...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Channels (only set what you enable)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABCDEF...
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=...
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
# SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-...

# Optional channel env fallbacks
# MATTERMOST_BOT_TOKEN=...
# MATTERMOST_URL=https://chat.example.com
# ZALO_BOT_TOKEN=...
# OPENCLAW_TWITCH_ACCESS_TOKEN=oauth:...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tools + voice/media (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BRAVE_API_KEY=...
# PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=pplx-...
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=...

# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=...
# XI_API_KEY=...  # alias for ElevenLabs
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Commercial real-estate (CRE) skills — Stockton's fork
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These power the CRE skill modules (crexi-sync, cold-outreach, prospect-research,
# property-analysis, underwriting-intake, listing-marketing-plan,
# just-listed-announcement, market-update-content, showing-management,
# signback-tracker, realnex-crm-commands). Fill in the ones for the skills you
# turn on. If a required value is blank, that skill will report as not-ready
# instead of running with a missing piece (e.g. sending outreach with a blank
# phone number). Values in [brackets] tell you where to get each one.

# RealNex CRM — used by ALL CRE skills. Your API key and API base URL.
# [Get from RealNex account settings / API section.]
# REALNEX_API_KEY=
# REALNEX_BASE_URL=https://api.realnex.com

# Your own contact details, inserted into outreach, intake forms, and invites
# sent to prospects. STOCKTON_PHONE is required by cold-outreach,
# just-listed-announcement, underwriting-intake, and showing-management — if it
# is blank those messages would go out with no callback number.
# STOCKTON_EMAIL=you@example.com
# STOCKTON_PHONE=+18015551234
# Your Telegram chat ID, so the assistant can text YOU briefings/alerts.
# [Message @userinfobot on Telegram to get your numeric chat ID.]
# STOCKTON_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# n8n automation webhooks — the URLs of your n8n workflows.
# CREXI_SYNC powers crexi-sync; SOCIAL_QUEUE powers just-listed-announcement and
# market-update-content. [Copy the Webhook node URL from each n8n workflow.]
# N8N_WEBHOOK_CREXI_SYNC=
# N8N_WEBHOOK_SOCIAL_QUEUE=

# Prospecting data — Apollo is the primary contact/email source (prospect-research).
# [Get from apollo.io account settings.]
# APOLLO_API_KEY=
# Hunter.io is an OPTIONAL fallback for email lookup when Apollo has no email.
# prospect-research still runs without it; set it only if you want the fallback.
# HUNTER_API_KEY=

# Google Calendar — used by showing-management to check availability and create
# invites. This is the path to your Google service-account credentials JSON file
# (not the JSON itself). [Create a service account in Google Cloud, download the
# key file, and put its path here.]
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_CREDENTIALS=~/.openclaw/google-calendar-credentials.json
